{"type":"standard","title":"Šeri and Ḫurri","displaytitle":"<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Šeri and Ḫurri</span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q22675267","titles":{"canonical":"Šeri_and_Ḫurri","normalized":"Šeri and Ḫurri","display":"<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Šeri and Ḫurri</span>"},"pageid":72670014,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1170005885","tid":"092c9ee1-3936-11ee-b034-821d63bb2d68","timestamp":"2023-08-12T17:31:14Z","description":"Pair of divine bulls in Hurrian mythology","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%A0eri_and_%E1%B8%AAurri","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%A0eri_and_%E1%B8%AAurri?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%A0eri_and_%E1%B8%AAurri?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:%C5%A0eri_and_%E1%B8%AAurri"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%A0eri_and_%E1%B8%AAurri","revisions":"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/%C5%A0eri_and_%E1%B8%AAurri","edit":"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%A0eri_and_%E1%B8%AAurri?action=edit","talk":"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:%C5%A0eri_and_%E1%B8%AAurri"}},"extract":"Šeri and Ḫurri were a pair of theriomorphic Hurrian gods who almost always appear together in known sources. They were believed to pull the chariot of Teššub, the Hurrian weather god. Šeri additionally could function as a deity mediating between petitioners and his master, but no individual role was ever assigned to Ḫurri. In addition to appearing in Hurrian offering lists and theophoric names, for example from Nuzi, Šeri and Ḫurri are also attested in Hittite and Mesopotamian sources. While the Hittites incorporated them into their pantheon alongside Teššub and other deities from his circle, in Mesopotamia they instead came to be associated with Adad.","extract_html":"<p><b>Šeri and Ḫurri</b> were a pair of theriomorphic Hurrian gods who almost always appear together in known sources. They were believed to pull the chariot of Teššub, the Hurrian weather god. Šeri additionally could function as a deity mediating between petitioners and his master, but no individual role was ever assigned to Ḫurri. In addition to appearing in Hurrian offering lists and theophoric names, for example from Nuzi, Šeri and Ḫurri are also attested in Hittite and Mesopotamian sources. While the Hittites incorporated them into their pantheon alongside Teššub and other deities from his circle, in Mesopotamia they instead came to be associated with Adad.</p>"}